From: buntOS contributors
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: regulator: Document MediaTek MT6368 PMIC Regulators

Add a binding for the regulators of the MediaTek MT6368 SPMI PMIC, which
board designs with the MT6897 (Dimensity 8300) SoC pair with the MT6363.
As with the MT6363 and MT6373 regulators, they are a child node of the
PMIC whose reg is the base of their registers.

The MT6368 has six bucks, a buck for an RF power amplifier (vpa) and
fifteen LDOs. VMCH can also be switched on and off by an external
interrupt, such as the card detect line of an SD card slot, through
vmch-eint-high or vmch-eint-low. As in the MediaTek driver, the SIM card
and DRAM LDOs are left out. Unlike the MT6363 binding, the bucks do not
list the ultra low power mode, which neither the MediaTek driver nor this
one can set.

---
 .../regulator/mediatek,mt6368-regulator.yaml  | 88 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 88 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/regulator/mediatek,mt6368-regulator.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/regulator/mediatek,mt6368-regulator.yaml
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..ffacaaf
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/regulator/mediatek,mt6368-regulator.yaml
@@ -0,0 +1,88 @@
+# SPDX-License-Identifier: (GPL-2.0-only OR BSD-2-Clause)
+%YAML 1.2
+---
+$id: http://devicetree.org/schemas/regulator/mediatek,mt6368-regulator.yaml#
+$schema: http://devicetree.org/meta-schemas/core.yaml#
+
+title: MediaTek MT6368 PMIC Regulators
+
+maintainers:
+  - buntOS contributors <buntos@localhost>
+
+description:
+  The MT6368 SPMI PMIC provides six BUCK regulators, a BUCK for an RF power
+  amplifier (vpa) and LDO (Low DropOut) regulators, and can optionally
+  provide overcurrent warnings with one ocp interrupt for each of them.
+  VMCH can also be switched on and off by an external interrupt, such as
+  the card detect line of an SD card slot, through vmch-eint-high or
+  vmch-eint-low, named after the active level of that interrupt.
+
+properties:
+  compatible:
+    const: mediatek,mt6368-regulator
+
+  reg:
+    maxItems: 1
+
+patternProperties:
+  "^v(buck[1-6]|pa)$":
+    description: Buck regulators
+    type: object
+    $ref: regulator.yaml#
+    unevaluatedProperties: false
+    properties:
+      regulator-allowed-modes:
+        description: |
+          Allowed Buck regulator operating modes allowed. Valid values below.
+            0 - Normal mode with automatic power saving, reducing the switching
+                frequency when light load conditions are detected
+            1 - Forced Continuous Conduction mode (FCCM) for improved voltage
+                regulation accuracy with constant switching frequency but lower
+                regulator efficiency
+            2 - Forced Low Power mode for improved regulator efficiency, used
+                when no heavy load is expected, does not limit the maximum out
+                current but unless only a light load is applied, there will be
+                regulation accuracy and efficiency losses.
+        maxItems: 3
+        items:
+          enum: [ 0, 1, 2 ]
+
+  "^v(ant|aud|aux)18$":
+    $ref: "#/$defs/ldo-common"
+
+  "^v(cn33-[12]|efuse|fp|ibr|io28|tp|usb)$":
+    $ref: "#/$defs/ldo-common"
+
+  "^vmc(h)?$":
+    $ref: "#/$defs/ldo-common"
+
+  "^vmch-eint-(high|low)$":
+    $ref: "#/$defs/ldo-common"
+
+  "^vrf1[38]-aif$":
+    $ref: "#/$defs/ldo-common"
+
+$defs:
+  ldo-common:
+    type: object
+    $ref: regulator.yaml#
+    unevaluatedProperties: false
+    properties:
+      regulator-allowed-modes:
+        description: |
+          Allowed LDO regulator operating modes allowed. Valid values below.
+            0 - Normal mode with automatic power saving, reducing the switching
+                frequency when light load conditions are detected
+            2 - Forced Low Power mode for improved regulator efficiency, used
+                when no heavy load is expected, does not limit the maximum out
+                current but unless only a light load is applied, there will be
+                regulation accuracy and efficiency losses.
+        maxItems: 2
+        items:
+          enum: [ 0, 2 ]
+
+required:
+  - compatible
+  - reg
+
+additionalProperties: false
